# Sample Package Manifest

File: opm/examples/manifest.oot

A package manifest is `ooda.pkg` at the project root. key=value lines.

```
name=hello-world
version=1.2.3
deps=json-parser,http-client
caps=FsRead,FsWrite
license=MIT
payload=hello-world.oo
commit=
sha256=
sig=
```

## Field Semantics

- `name`: unique package name.
- `version`: Semantic Version (major.minor.patch).
- `caps`: capability names the package needs.
- `deps`: comma-separated names or `path:` / `git:` specs.
- `sha256`: expected CAS hash of the payload, verified at install.
